{"name":"Copacabana","hex":"#006c8d","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Copacabana","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["A neighborhood of Zona Sul district, Rio de Janeiro, Rio de Janeiro state, Brazil","The main beach in Rio de Janeiro, located in the eponymous district."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A beached area known for partying."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Copacabana"}],"entries":[{"title":"Copacabana, Rio de Janeiro","blocks":[{"text":"Copacabana is a Brazilian bairro (neighbourhood) located in the South Zone of the city of Rio de Janeiro, Brazil. It is most prominently known for its 4 km (2.5 mile) balneario beach, which is one of the most famous in the world."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/62/Praia_de_Copacabana_-_Rio_de_Janeiro%2C_Brasil.jpg/330px-Praia_de_Copacabana_-_Rio_de_Janeiro%2C_Brasil.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Copacabana%2C_Rio_de_Janeiro","wikidata":"Q202730"},{"title":"Copacabana (nightclub)","blocks":[{"text":"The Copacabana is a New York City nightclub that has existed in several locations. In earlier locations, many entertainers, such as Danny Thomas, Pat Cooper, and the comedy team of Martin and Lewis, made their New York debuts at the Copacabana. The Barry Manilow song \"Copacabana\" (1978) is named after, and set in, the club. The nightclub was used as a setting in the films Goodfellas, Raging Bull, Tootsie, The Purple Rose of Cairo, Carlito's Way, Lonely Boy, The French Connection, Martin and Lewis, Green Book, Beyond the Sea, The Irishman, and One Night in Miami. It was also used in several plays, including Barry Manilow's Copacabana. The musical film Copacabana (1947), starring Groucho Marx and Carmen Miranda, takes place in the Copacabana, as does the made-for-television film based on the Manilow song, in which Manilow himself starred."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/0/05/CopacabanaLogo.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Copacabana_(nightclub)","wikidata":"Q1130938"},{"title":"Copacabana (song)","blocks":[{"text":"\"Copacabana\", also known as \"Copacabana (At the Copa)\", is a song recorded by Barry Manilow. Written by Manilow, Jack Feldman, and Bruce Sussman, it was released in 1978 as the third single from Manilow's fifth studio album, Even Now (1978). The same year, \"Copacabana\" appeared in the soundtrack album of the film Foul Play."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/35/Copacabana_barry_manilow_US_single_long_version_var_A.webp/330px-Copacabana_barry_manilow_US_single_long_version_var_A.webp?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Copacabana_(song)","wikidata":"Q1130943"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/db/Bairros_de_Copacabana_e_Leme%2C_early_20th_century.tif/lossless-page1-500px-Bairros_de_Copacabana_e_Leme%2C_early_20th_century.tif.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/db/Bairros_de_Copacabana_e_Leme%2C_early_20th_century.tif/lossless-page1-1280px-Bairros_de_Copacabana_e_Leme%2C_early_20th_century.tif.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/db/Bairros_de_Copacabana_e_Leme%2C_early_20th_century.tif/lossless-page1-500px-Bairros_de_Copacabana_e_Leme%2C_early_20th_century.tif.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Copacabana, early 20th century","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ABairros_de_Copacabana_e_Leme%2C_early_20th_century.tif"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1d/Copacabana_Beach_1971.j